// ttyAt is the center dot's code and case, typed before a TTPFX entry.
ttyAt, 0140

// ttyIn holds, by concise code with 0100 added in upper case, the ASCII
// character a typed key reads as, 0 for none.
// RETURN reads as LF and backspace as itself, RUBOUT; the stand-ins read as what they
